iew#status-areas","content":"History","locale":"en"},"2951":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"View recent failure phases, exit codes, and associated task output","locale":"en"},"2952":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#status-areas","content":"The installation lifecycle indicates whether the instance files are ready. Runtime status indicates whether the WebUI process is currently running. A new launch can start only when the lifecycle is “Ready” and the WebUI is not running.","locale":"en"},"2953":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#check-readiness","content":"Confirm that the installation lifecycle is “Ready,” the Python and Core paths exist, and no task is currently reinstalling the instance, restoring PyTorch, or installing a model-library item.","locale":"en"},"2954":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#select-launch","content":"The launch task opens in Task Center. The app checks the environment, PyTorch, extension conflicts, and launch arguments. If a choice is required, a launch-decision dialog appears.","locale":"en"},"2955":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#handle-launch-decisions","content":"Follow the dialog to handle incompatible extensions, PyTorch, or launch arguments. Closing the decision dialog does not fix the problem automatically. After cancelling, you can adjust the configuration in the corresponding management section.","locale":"en"},"2956":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#wait-for-address-capture","content":"After runtime status becomes “Running,” continue to wait for “Captured WebUI Address” to appear. Successful capture means the app has identified the WebUI's access entry point.","locale":"en"},"2957":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"After selecting “Stop,” wait for runtime status to return to “Not Running.” Do not repeatedly select Launch while the process is stopping.","locale":"en"},"2958":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"“View Launch Task” opens the phases and output of the current launch. “View Logs” in error history opens the exact task in which that error occurred.","locale":"en"},"2959":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"“Show in File Manager” opens the instance root, not the Core or model directory.","locale":"en"},"2960":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"If the WebUI is running but has no address, inspect the launch output for the listening address, port conflicts, and browser connection status.","locale":"en"},"2961":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"When status is “Awaiting Launch Decision,” handle the current decision before creating another launch task.","locale":"en"},"2962":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"After the process enters the running state, the WebUI may still be loading models or initializing\nservices. Rely on the captured address and task output. Troubleshoot the launch logs only if the\nprocess exists but no address appears for an extended period.","locale":"en"},"2963":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-overview-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-overview","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-overview#stop-and-troubleshoot","content":"To change launch arguments, read Launch Configuration. To inspect Python or Git, use the Instance Terminal.","locale":"en"},"2964":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"page","content":"Component Paths","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","locale":"en"},"2965":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Understand the differences between the instance root, Python, and Core, and safely update component references.","locale":"en"},"2966":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#change-the-python-or-core-path","content":"Change the Python or Core path","locale":"en"},"2967":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#stop-related-operations","content":"Stop related operations","locale":"en"},"2968":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#check-the-target-directories","content":"Check the target directories","locale":"en"},"2969":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#select-and-apply","content":"Select and apply","locale":"en"},"2970":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#handle-a-stale-configuration-warning","content":"Handle a stale configuration warning","locale":"en"},"2971":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#verify-the-new-environment","content":"Verify the new environment","locale":"en"},"2972":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Which feature should you use?","locale":"en"},"2973":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"An instance contains three distinct locations. The instance root is the boundary of the complete instance, the Python directory contains its standalone runtime environment, and the Core directory contains the WebUI code. Python and Core can be inside the instance root, or they can refer to external directories after an import or system scan.","locale":"en"},"2974":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Path","locale":"en"},"2975":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Purpose","locale":"en"},"2976":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Editable from “Component Paths”","locale":"en"},"2977":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Instance root","locale":"en"},"2978":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"File boundary of the complete instance","locale":"en"},"2979":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"No; use instance migration","locale":"en"},"2980":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Python directory","locale":"en"},"2981":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Standalone Python and installed packages","locale":"en"},"2982":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"2983":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Core directory","locale":"en"},"2984":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"WebUI code, extensions, and related resources","locale":"en"},"2985":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths","content":"Yes","locale":"en"},"2986":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#stop-related-operations","content":"Stop the WebUI first, and wait for installation, version, extension, snapshot, and model tasks to finish. Updating paths requires exclusive access to the current instance. The app may also stop related runtime resources before the update.","locale":"en"},"2987":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#check-the-target-directories","content":"The Python directory must be a usable standalone Python environment. The Core directory must match the current WebUI type. Do not select a drive root, a user home directory, or a directory already used by another instance.","locale":"en"},"2988":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#select-and-apply","content":"Enter or choose the new directories under “Component Paths,” confirm that neither value is empty, and select “Apply.” The backend validates the paths, instance overlap, and component types.","locale":"en"},"2989":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#handle-a-stale-configuration-warning","content":"If the page reports that the instance configuration has changed, select “Reload,” choose the directories again, and resubmit. Do not use a stale page to overwrite configuration just saved by another management operation.","locale":"en"},"2990":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#verify-the-new-environment","content":"Return to “Instance Information” and check the Python version and Core path. Then run version checks in the Instance Terminal, and finally launch the WebUI again.","locale":"en"},"2991":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#verify-the-new-environment","content":"The app only updates the component references in the instance record. It does not copy or move the\nold directory to the new location. To relocate the complete instance, use “Migrate Instance” in\nInstance Maintenance.","locale":"en"},"2992":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Goal","locale":"en"},"2993":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Correct operation","locale":"en"},"2994":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Refer to another existing Python/Core","locale":"en"},"2995":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Change component paths","locale":"en"},"2996":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Move the complete instance root to another drive","locale":"en"},"2997":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Migrate the instance","locale":"en"},"2998":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Repair a missing or damaged Python/Core","locale":"en"},"2999":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Reinstall the instance","locale":"en"},"3000":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Restore a previously valid directory reference","locale":"en"},"3001":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-36","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"Change the component path back to the original directory","locale":"en"},"3002":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-paths-37","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-paths#which-feature-should-you-use","content":"External components are not moved automatically when you change paths, migrate, or delete an instance. If you later try to force-rebuild an external Python/Core, the backend refuses to delete a component outside the instance root. Plan a new managed directory first.","locale":"en"},"3003":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"page","content":"PyTorch Management","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","locale":"en"},"3004":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","content":"Check compatibility between the current PyTorch build and device, then reinstall automatically or manually.","locale":"en"},"3005":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Understand the check result","locale":"en"},"3006":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#reinstall-pytorch","content":"Reinstall PyTorch","locale":"en"},"3007":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#stop-the-webui","content":"Stop the WebUI","locale":"en"},"3008":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#choose-how-to-select-a-version","content":"Choose how to select a version","locale":"en"},"3009":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#decide-whether-to-force-reinstallation","content":"Decide whether to force reinstallation","locale":"en"},"3010":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#confirm-and-wait-for-the-task","content":"Confirm and wait for the task","locale":"en"},"3011":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result","locale":"en"},"3012":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"Handle failures","locale":"en"},"3013":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","content":"The “PyTorch” page inspects Torch components in the instance Python environment, detects the device type, and lists installation combinations supported by the current WebUI. Options vary by WebUI, operating system, and hardware.","locale":"en"},"3014":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Status","locale":"en"},"3015":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"3016":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Compatible","locale":"en"},"3017":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"The current build matches the detected device and WebUI rules","locale":"en"},"3018":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Incompatible","locale":"en"},"3019":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"The installed build does not match the device or supported combinations","locale":"en"},"3020":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Not Installed","locale":"en"},"3021":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Required PyTorch packages were not detected in the instance environment","locale":"en"},"3022":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Unable to Check","locale":"en"},"3023":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"Python, the management API, or an environment query failed","locale":"en"},"3024":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#understand-the-check-result","content":"The page also shows detected versions of Torch, TorchVision, TorchAudio, xFormers, and other components, along with the recommended device build. Rely on the catalog currently shown on this page; do not copy installation commands from a guide for another WebUI.","locale":"en"},"3025":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#stop-the-webui","content":"Reinstalling PyTorch modifies the active Python environment, so stop the WebUI first. The app coordinates the management API; you do not need to terminate it manually.","locale":"en"},"3026":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#choose-how-to-select-a-version","content":"Most users should choose “Select Automatically,” allowing the installation task to determine the combination from the hardware. Use “Select Manually” only when you clearly understand your driver, CUDA, ROCm, or CPU requirements.","locale":"en"},"3027":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#decide-whether-to-force-reinstallation","content":"When the current status is already compatible, normally leave “Reinstall Even If the Current Version Is Correct” disabled. Enable it only for damaged files, dependency problems, or redeploying the same build.","locale":"en"},"3028":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#confirm-and-wait-for-the-task","content":"Select “Reinstall PyTorch,” confirm the operation, and follow dependency download, installation, and environment-check output in the bottom-right status area or Task Center.","locale":"en"},"3029":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#verify-the-result","content":"After the task completes, refresh this page, confirm that status is “Compatible,” and check the installed build. Then launch the WebUI for an actual runtime verification.","locale":"en"},"3030":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"If automatic selection fails, check the graphics driver, operating-system support, and detected device reported by the page. Do not try several CUDA/ROCm builds at random.","locale":"en"},"3031":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"If package downloads or resolution fail, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors.","locale":"en"},"3032":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"If the result remains incompatible after installation, open the latest task output and record the selected build, exit code, and environment-check result.","locale":"en"},"3033":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"If a PyTorch decision dialog appears during launch, you can cancel and return here to fix the environment. Use “Ignore and Launch” only when you accept the risk for this run.","locale":"en"},"3034":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-pytorch#handle-failures","content":"This operation modifies PyTorch and its supporting packages in the current instance Python\nenvironment. Do not install Torch manually in the Instance Terminal at the same time, and do not\nlaunch the WebUI before the task completes.","locale":"en"},"3035":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"page","content":"Snapshot Management","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","locale":"en"},"3036":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","content":"Create environment snapshots, preview restoration effects, and safely restore or delete snapshots.","locale":"en"},"3037":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#create-and-inspect-snapshots","content":"Create and inspect snapshots","locale":"en"},"3038":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Restoration options","locale":"en"},"3039":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#preview-and-restore","content":"Preview and restore","locale":"en"},"3040":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#prepare-for-restoration","content":"Prepare for restoration","locale":"en"},"3041":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#open-the-restore-dialog","content":"Open the restore dialog","locale":"en"},"3042":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#read-the-blockers","content":"Read the blockers","locale":"en"},"3043":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#review-planned-changes","content":"Review planned changes","locale":"en"},"3044":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#confirm-restoration","content":"Confirm restoration","locale":"en"},"3045":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#verify-after-completion","content":"Verify after completion","locale":"en"},"3046":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","content":"A snapshot records the WebUI type, Core commit, Python packages, and extension state so you can restore the environment after version, dependency, or extension changes. Package information is included by default when a snapshot is created.","locale":"en"},"3047":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","content":"Snapshots usually do not include models, generated images, arbitrary user files, or a complete\ncopy of uncommitted code. Back up this content separately before high-risk operations.","locale":"en"},"3048":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#create-and-inspect-snapshots","content":"Wait for completion in the bottom-right status area or Task Center. Do not reinstall or restore\nthe environment while a snapshot is being created.","locale":"en"},"3049":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#create-and-inspect-snapshots","content":"Refresh the list, expand the new snapshot, and check its creation time, package count, extension\ncount, and Core commit.","locale":"en"},"3050":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#create-and-inspect-snapshots","content":"A malformed snapshot displays a parsing error and cannot be restored directly. Deleting a snapshot permanently deletes only the corresponding snapshot file; it does not change the current environment.","locale":"en"},"3051":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"3052":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"When disabled","locale":"en"},"3053":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"When enabled","locale":"en"},"3054":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Clean extra packages","locale":"en"},"3055":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Restore recorded packages and keep packages added after the snapshot","locale":"en"},"3056":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Uninstall packages not recorded in the snapshot","locale":"en"},"3057":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Clean extra extensions","locale":"en"},"3058":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Restore recorded extensions and keep extensions added after the snapshot","locale":"en"},"3059":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Delete extensions not recorded in the snapshot","locale":"en"},"3060":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Force Git reset","locale":"en"},"3061":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-25","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Uncommitted changes may block restoration","locale":"en"},"3062":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-26","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Discard uncommitted changes in the WebUI and extension repositories, then switch to the recorded commits","locale":"en"},"3063":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-27","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#restoration-options","content":"Some snapshots mark an option as “Required.” Restoration cannot begin until every required option is enabled.","locale":"en"},"3064":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-28","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#prepare-for-restoration","content":"Stop the WebUI, wait for version, extension, model, PyTorch, and other management tasks to finish, and back up uncommitted code and important files.","locale":"en"},"3065":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-29","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#open-the-restore-dialog","content":"Select “Restore” on the target snapshot. After you choose cleanup and Git-reset options, the app automatically generates a restoration preview bound to the current instance state.","locale":"en"},"3066":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-30","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#read-the-blockers","content":"A mismatched type, missing Core, uncommitted repository changes, or another unresolved problem blocks restoration. Follow the instructions or enable the required options, then wait for the preview to be analyzed again automatically.","locale":"en"},"3067":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-31","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#review-planned-changes","content":"Inspect added, removed, updated, skipped, and unchanged items separately for repositories, Python packages, and extensions. Do not rely only on the total number of changes.","locale":"en"},"3068":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-32","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#confirm-restoration","content":"You can submit only while the current preview is restorable. After the task is accepted, the restore dialog closes. Follow subsequent phases and output in the bottom-right status area and Task Center.","locale":"en"},"3069":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-33","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#verify-after-completion","content":"Refresh the Versions, Extensions, and PyTorch pages, then launch the WebUI. Verify models and user files against their separate backups.","locale":"en"},"3070":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-34","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#verify-after-completion","content":"The preview is bound to the snapshot, restoration options, management API state, and instance configuration. If you change paths, launch configuration, or other instance settings after preview generation, the old preview becomes invalid. Close the dialog and generate a new one instead of attempting another submission.","locale":"en"},"3071":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots-35","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-snapshots#verify-after-completion","content":"“Clean Extra Packages,” “Clean Extra Extensions,” and “Force Git Reset” can all remove content\nfrom the current environment that the snapshot does not preserve. Restore only after checking both\nthe preview lists and your independent backups.","locale":"en"},"3072":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","type":"page","content":"Instance Terminal","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","locale":"en"},"3073":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","content":"Run inspection or maintenance commands with the current instance's Python, Git, and managed environment.","locale":"en"},"3074":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#open-and-inspect-the-environment","content":"Open and inspect the environment","locale":"en"},"3075":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Session operations","locale":"en"},"3076":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"Use the terminal safely","locale":"en"},"3077":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","content":"The Instance Terminal uses the current instance's working directory and managed environment, and places standalone Python, Git, and Micromamba/Conda tools in the correct order on `PATH`. The general application terminal is not automatically bound to an instance. Prefer the Instance Terminal when diagnosing a WebUI.","locale":"en"},"3078":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#open-and-inspect-the-environment","content":"When you enter “Run → Terminal,” the app creates or resubscribes to the current instance's terminal session and restores retained output. You can enter commands after status becomes “Running.”","locale":"en"},"3079":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#open-and-inspect-the-environment","content":"Common read-only checks:","locale":"en"},"3080":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#open-and-inspect-the-environment","content":"You can also run `git status` in the Core repository to inspect uncommitted changes. Path presentation and directory-changing commands depend on the shell in use on Windows, macOS, or Linux.","locale":"en"},"3081":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Operation","locale":"en"},"3082":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"3083":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Leave the section","locale":"en"},"3084":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Unsubscribe the current interface; this must not be treated as ending the process","locale":"en"},"3085":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Restart terminal","locale":"en"},"3086":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"End the current PTY and create a new terminal session for the same instance","locale":"en"},"3087":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Close terminal","locale":"en"},"3088":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Confirm termination and release the current terminal process","locale":"en"},"3089":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Re-enter","locale":"en"},"3090":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"Subscribe to the existing session, restore retained output, and continue receiving new output","locale":"en"},"3091":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#session-operations","content":"You can restart a terminal whose status is “Exited.” When status is “Close Failed,” the backend still retains the cleanup obligation for the original session. Use “Close Terminal Process” again instead of creating replacement sessions repeatedly.","locale":"en"},"3092":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"Before running install, delete, move, or Git commands, confirm the current directory and target path.","locale":"en"},"3093":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"Do not manually install packages while the WebUI, a version update, snapshot restoration, or reinstallation task is changing the same environment.","locale":"en"},"3094":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-21","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"Prefer `python -m <module>` so the command uses the module associated with the current instance's Python.","locale":"en"},"3095":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-22","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"Manual terminal changes do not create a snapshot automatically and are not guaranteed to be reversible by Hanafubuki.","locale":"en"},"3096":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-23","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"When changing supported extensions, models, versions, or PyTorch, prefer the corresponding management page so task status and error output are available.","locale":"en"},"3097":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal-24","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-terminal","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-terminal#use-the-terminal-safely","content":"The Instance Terminal is not a simulated environment. Deleting directories, resetting Git, or\nreinstalling packages changes the instance directly. Create a snapshot before important\noperations, and back up models, outputs, and custom code separately.","locale":"en"},"3098":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"page","content":"WebUI Variants","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","locale":"en"},"3099":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"Switch preset repositories and branches on supported instances, and synchronize reinstallation configuration.","locale":"en"},"3100":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#switch-variants","content":"Switch variants","locale":"en"},"3101":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#back-up-the-current-state","content":"Back up the current state","locale":"en"},"3102":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#stop-the-webui","content":"Stop the WebUI","locale":"en"},"3103":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#check-the-target-source","content":"Check the target source","locale":"en"},"3104":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#select-switch-and-confirm","content":"Select “Switch” and confirm","locale":"en"},"3105":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#verify-the-variant","content":"Verify the variant","locale":"en"},"3106":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#synchronize-only-the-reinstallation-configuration","content":"Synchronize only the reinstallation configuration","locale":"en"},"3107":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"A WebUI variant is a set of repository, branch, and submodule settings provided by the current WebUI. It differs from an ordinary branch switch: changing the variant can replace the Git remote and determines which source a later Core reinstallation uses.","locale":"en"},"3108":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"The page marks two values separately:","locale":"en"},"3109":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"“Current”: the variant that actually matches the Core repository now;","locale":"en"},"3110":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"“Reinstallation”: the variant saved in the instance record and used for future reinstalls.","locale":"en"},"3111":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants","content":"When the two values differ, the page offers to synchronize the reinstallation setting.","locale":"en"},"3112":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#back-up-the-current-state","content":"Create a snapshot, and separately back up uncommitted code, extension configuration, and important user files. Switching variants may forcibly change the working tree.","locale":"en"},"3113":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#stop-the-webui","content":"The WebUI must be stopped before switching variants. Wait until runtime status in “Instance Information” returns to “Not Running.”","locale":"en"},"3114":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#check-the-target-source","content":"Review the variant name, repository URL, branch, and whether it includes submodules. Do not assume from the name alone that it is compatible with your current extensions or model workflows.","locale":"en"},"3115":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#select-switch-and-confirm","content":"The confirmation dialog shows the repository and branch again. After you accept, the app starts a version-switch task and, on success, saves that variant as the reinstallation configuration.","locale":"en"},"3116":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#verify-the-variant","content":"Refresh the page and confirm that “Current” and “Reinstallation” both point to the target variant. Then check the branch and commit on the Versions page before launching the WebUI.","locale":"en"},"3117":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#synchronize-only-the-reinstallation-configuration","content":"If you changed Core to a known variant by another method but “Reinstallation” still shows the old value, use “Synchronize Reinstallation Settings.” This changes only the variant used for future reinstalls; it does not switch the repository contents again.","locale":"en"},"3118":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#synchronize-only-the-reinstallation-configuration","content":"Switching variants may replace the remote repository and forcibly switch to the target branch.\nConfirmation in the interface is not a substitute for a backup. Commit changes you need to\npreserve to your own repository, or export them as a patch first.","locale":"en"},"3119":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-variants-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-variants","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-variants#synchronize-only-the-reinstallation-configuration","content":"To update or locate a commit within the same repository, use WebUI Versions.","locale":"en"},"3120":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"page","content":"WebUI Versions","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Instance Management"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions","locale":"en"},"3121":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-0","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions","content":"Update a WebUI, or switch branches, commits, and package versions on supported instances.","locale":"en"},"3122":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-1","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#git-based-webuis","content":"Git-based WebUIs","locale":"en"},"3123":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-2","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#create-a-snapshot-and-back-up-code","content":"Create a snapshot and back up code","locale":"en"},"3124":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-3","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#stop-the-webui","content":"Stop the WebUI","locale":"en"},"3125":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-4","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#choose-an-operation","content":"Choose an operation","locale":"en"},"3126":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-5","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#confirm-the-local-changes-warning","content":"Confirm the local-changes warning","locale":"en"},"3127":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-6","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#track-and-verify","content":"Track and verify","locale":"en"},"3128":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-7","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"InvokeAI package versions","locale":"en"},"3129":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-8","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions","content":"The “Versions” page varies by WebUI type. Git-based instances such as Stable Diffusion WebUI, ComfyUI, Fooocus, and SD Trainer show repository branches and commits. InvokeAI shows installed and available package versions.","locale":"en"},"3130":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-9","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#git-based-webuis","content":"The page shows the current branch, commit, commit date, and the number of commits ahead of or behind the remote branch. Update notices may also summarize available extension and PyTorch updates.","locale":"en"},"3131":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-10","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#create-a-snapshot-and-back-up-code","content":"Create an environment snapshot first. If you have modified Core files, also copy a patch, commit the changes to a personal branch, or back them up separately. Snapshot restoration and some switch operations can reset the Git working tree.","locale":"en"},"3132":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-11","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#stop-the-webui","content":"Ordinary version operations do not always require a stopped process, but changing code after stopping it makes it easier to ensure that the next launch uses one consistent set of files.","locale":"en"},"3133":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-12","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#choose-an-operation","content":"“Update Current Branch” fetches and updates the current branch. “Switch Branch” selects a local or remote branch. The commit list lets you locate and switch to a specific commit. Reload branches or commits first when you need the latest remote data.","locale":"en"},"3134":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-13","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#confirm-the-local-changes-warning","content":"If the repository contains uncommitted changes, the interface asks for confirmation. Continuing does not guarantee that those changes will be preserved. Cancel and back them up first if loss or conflicts would be unacceptable.","locale":"en"},"3135":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-14","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#track-and-verify","content":"Wait for the task to finish in the bottom-right status area or Task Center. Refresh the Versions page to confirm the new branch and commit, then launch the WebUI and check extension and dependency compatibility.","locale":"en"},"3136":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-15","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"The InvokeAI Versions page shows the current version, latest stable version, available versions, and prerelease labels. Selecting a version installs that version. “Upgrade” installs the target version determined by the current rules.","locale":"en"},"3137":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-16","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"Prefer the latest stable version unless you need to test new features. Do not select a version marked “Prerelease” otherwise.","locale":"en"},"3138":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-17","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"Package installation modifies the instance Python environment. Stop the WebUI first, then check PyTorch and launch status after the task finishes.","locale":"en"},"3139":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-18","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"If the list is empty or fails to refresh, check the network, PyPI mirror, and instance management API.","locale":"en"},"3140":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-19","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"Git operations manage only the code repository. They do not protect models, outputs,\nconfiguration, or uncommitted code. Prepare both an environment snapshot and a separate file\nbackup before switching.","locale":"en"},"3141":{"id":"/en/docs/instance-versions-20","page_id":"/en/docs/instance-versions","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/instance-versions#invokeai-package-versions","content":"To change a preset repository-and-branch combination, read WebUI Variants.","locale":"en"},"3142":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"page","content":"Quick start","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Getting Started"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start","locale":"en"},"3143":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-0","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start","content":"Create and launch your first WebUI instance with the shortest workflow.","locale":"en"},"3144":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-1","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#wait-for-the-runtime-environment","content":"Wait for the runtime environment","locale":"en"},"3145":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-2","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#add-an-instance","content":"Add an instance","locale":"en"},"3146":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-3","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#complete-the-installation","content":"Complete the installation","locale":"en"},"3147":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-4","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#launch-the-webui","content":"Launch the WebUI","locale":"en"},"3148":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-5","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/quick-start#manage-the-instance","content":"Manage the instance","locale":"en"},"3149":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-6","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#wait-for-the-runtime-environment","content":"On the first launch, wait for Python, Micromamba, and Git to finish preparing. If a runtime environment error appears at the top of the window or on Home, go to “Settings → Runtime Environment” first.","locale":"en"},"3150":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-7","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#add-an-instance","content":"Select “Add Instance” on Home. New users will usually choose “New Installation.” If you already have a WebUI, choose “Import Existing Instance” or “Scan System.”","locale":"en"},"3151":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-8","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#complete-the-installation","content":"Select the WebUI type and installation directory. Keep the default Python, PyTorch, and branch settings to get started. Installation progress takes over the instance workspace and provides task output, cancellation, and retry after failure.","locale":"en"},"3152":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-9","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#launch-the-webui","content":"Open the instance and select Launch from the overview or workspace. Once an address is captured, you can open the WebUI directly. To adjust arguments, go to “Run → Launch.”","locale":"en"},"3153":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-10","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#manage-the-instance","content":"Use Instance Management to maintain versions, extensions, models, snapshots, and paths. Long-running tasks are reported in the bottom-right status area. You can also open Task Center from the title bar to inspect their output.","locale":"en"},"3154":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-11","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#manage-the-instance","content":"<Card title=\"Installation methods\" href=\"/docs/webui-install\" description=\"Compare a new installation, import, system scan, and snapshot recovery.\" />","locale":"en"},"3155":{"id":"/en/docs/quick-start-12","page_id":"/en/docs/quick-start","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/quick-start#manage-the-instance","content":"<Card title=\"Instance Management\" href=\"/docs/instance-management\" description=\"Learn about every management section available for an instance.\" />","locale":"en"},"3156":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","type":"page","content":"About and Updates","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","locale":"en"},"3157":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","content":"View the application version and project links, and check for updates.","locale":"en"},"3158":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Checking for updates","locale":"en"},"3159":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#installing-a-signed-update","content":"Installing a signed update","locale":"en"},"3160":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Updating the portable edition","locale":"en"},"3161":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","content":"The **About** page shows the current Hanafubuki version and links to the project repository, author, and related WebUI documentation. External links open in the system browser rather than replacing the application window.","locale":"en"},"3162":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"In non-portable mode, the application checks for updates periodically in the background. You can also click **Check for updates** on the About page to check immediately. Progress and results appear in the lower-right corner of the settings window.","locale":"en"},"3163":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"An update check can have three outcomes:","locale":"en"},"3164":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"3165":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Next step","locale":"en"},"3166":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Signed update available","locale":"en"},"3167":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"The application has downloaded and verified an update for the current installation type; confirm installation and restart","locale":"en"},"3168":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Manual installer available","locale":"en"},"3169":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Automatic updating is unavailable or verification failed; choose an installer for the current platform and download it in the browser","locale":"en"},"3170":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"Up to date or unavailable","locale":"en"},"3171":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"No action is needed, or inspect the network, proxy, and update source according to the error","locale":"en"},"3172":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#checking-for-updates","content":"The manual installer list includes only verified, available types for the current platform and marks the recommended option. Clicking Download opens a retained release address; the interface does not accept arbitrary download URLs.","locale":"en"},"3173":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#installing-a-signed-update","content":"Click **Check for updates** and wait for the check, download, and signature verification to\nfinish.","locale":"en"},"3174":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#installing-a-signed-update","content":"Allow the application to shut down in order; do not force-terminate it while the installer is\nrunning.","locale":"en"},"3175":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#installing-a-signed-update","content":"After the application restarts, return to **About**, confirm the new version, and inspect the\nruntime state.","locale":"en"},"3176":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#installing-a-signed-update","content":"If automatic installation fails, the application attempts to provide a manual installer. Exit the application completely before installing it normally for the current platform; do not run the old application and installer at the same time.","locale":"en"},"3177":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Launcher portable mode does not perform in-app automatic updates. When you check for updates, the interface directs you to replace the portable package manually.","locale":"en"},"3178":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Download the latest portable Launcher from the project website and verify its platform and\narchitecture.","locale":"en"},"3179":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Back up the portable data directory. Do not delete its configuration, instance records, or user\ndata.","locale":"en"},"3180":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Extract the new package, replace the program files, and start it with the original data\nlocation.","locale":"en"},"3181":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-about-updates#updating-the-portable-edition","content":"Windows, Linux, and macOS can all keep program or runtime files in use while the process is\nrunning. Exit normally and confirm that the process has ended before installing or replacing a\nportable package.","locale":"en"},"3182":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"page","content":"Agent Settings","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent","locale":"en"},"3183":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent","content":"Configure models, permissions, memory, network tools, MCP, and Skills.","locale":"en"},"3184":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Recommended configuration order","locale":"en"},"3185":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#add-a-provider-and-choose-a-model","content":"Add a provider and choose a model","locale":"en"},"3186":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#choose-a-permission-mode","content":"Choose a permission mode","locale":"en"},"3187":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#decide-whether-to-use-memory","content":"Decide whether to use memory","locale":"en"},"3188":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#configure-built-in-network-tools","content":"Configure built-in network tools","locale":"en"},"3189":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#add-mcp-and-skills-as-needed","content":"Add MCP and Skills as needed","locale":"en"},"3190":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"Saving and scope of effect","locale":"en"},"3191":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"Continue reading","locale":"en"},"3192":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent","content":"Agent settings are organized from top to bottom into Models and Providers, Behavior and Memory, Built-in Network Tools, MCP, and Skills. Before using the Agent, configure at least one enabled model provider. You can choose a model globally or select one for an individual session after creating it.","locale":"en"},"3193":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#add-a-provider-and-choose-a-model","content":"Add a provider matching the server protocol, enter its API address and credentials, and save. After enabling the provider, choose the default provider and model in the separate model policy, then configure reasoning effort, context window, image input, and compaction policy.","locale":"en"},"3194":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#choose-a-permission-mode","content":"**Manual** or **Auto review** is recommended for first use. **Full access** reduces approvals and the application provides no operating-system sandbox protection. It requires another confirmation in the interface and should be enabled only for trusted directories and clearly scoped tasks.","locale":"en"},"3195":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#decide-whether-to-use-memory","content":"Memory can remain disabled by default. If you enable it, separately decide whether to read memory, generate it from sessions, and exclude external content. Resetting clears existing memory, so confirm that you no longer need it first.","locale":"en"},"3196":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#configure-built-in-network-tools","content":"Choose DuckDuckGo, SearXNG, or automatic search, and configure the SearXNG address and Jina Reader fallback as needed. Network search and fetch policies take effect after a restart.","locale":"en"},"3197":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#add-mcp-and-skills-as-needed","content":"Connect only trusted MCP servers and grant tools the minimum permissions. Review a Skill's instructions, scripts, and resources before installation. When finished, create a test session to verify the actual capabilities.","locale":"en"},"3198":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"The model policy and provider list have separate save buttons; do not close the window while either has unsaved changes.","locale":"en"},"3199":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"Changes to the permission mode and memory switches are saved according to their regular setting behavior.","locale":"en"},"3200":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"MCP servers, MCP credentials, and Skills have their own management operations and are not part of the ordinary **Restore defaults** action.","locale":"en"},"3201":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"Sessions retain their own model and Skill state, and each model sampling step freezes the tool plan that existed at its start. After changing global settings, consult the relevant topic to determine whether a change applies on the current session's next turn or requires a new session.","locale":"en"},"3202":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#saving-and-scope-of-effect","content":"Provider tokens, custom authentication headers, and MCP credentials are sensitive. Do not place\nthem in prompts, project files, or screenshots. Diagnostics exclude known credential documents,\nbut do not redact every other collected item individually. Review a diagnostic bundle before\nsharing it.","locale":"en"},"3203":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Agent Quick Start\" href=\"/docs/agent\" description=\"Complete the first configuration and session.\" />","locale":"en"},"3204":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Providers and Models\" href=\"/docs/agent-providers-models\" description=\"Understand protocols, model capabilities, and context.\" />","locale":"en"},"3205":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Session Management\" href=\"/docs/agent-conversations\" description=\"Manage history, archiving, deletion, and forks.\" />","locale":"en"},"3206":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Permissions and Approvals\" href=\"/docs/agent-permissions\" description=\"Choose a permission mode and review operation targets.\" />","locale":"en"},"3207":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"MCP\" href=\"/docs/agent-mcp\" description=\"Configure external servers, connections, and tool policies.\" />","locale":"en"},"3208":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Skills\" href=\"/docs/agent-skills\" description=\"Install reusable workflows and select them for sessions.\" />","locale":"en"},"3209":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-agent-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-agent","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-agent#continue-reading","content":"<Card title=\"Memory\" href=\"/docs/agent-memory\" description=\"Manage retrieval, generation, contribution, and reset.\" />","locale":"en"},"3210":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"page","content":"Appearance","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","locale":"en"},"3211":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","content":"Configure the theme, accent color, wallpaper, and background effects.","locale":"en"},"3212":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#theme-and-accent-color","content":"Theme and accent color","locale":"en"},"3213":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adding-and-selecting-wallpaper","content":"Adding and selecting wallpaper","locale":"en"},"3214":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#import-images","content":"Import images","locale":"en"},"3215":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#check-import-results","content":"Check import results","locale":"en"},"3216":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#select-wallpaper","content":"Select wallpaper","locale":"en"},"3217":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#choose-fixed-or-random-wallpaper","content":"Choose fixed or random wallpaper","locale":"en"},"3218":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Adjusting background effects","locale":"en"},"3219":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","content":"Appearance settings affect only the interface. They do not modify instances, models, or the runtime. Theme and background changes apply immediately, so you can assess readability as you make adjustments.","locale":"en"},"3220":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#theme-and-accent-color","content":"The theme can **Follow system**, use **Light**, or use **Dark**. Follow system uses the operating system's current light or dark mode. A fixed theme is useful when the system theme changes often but you want the application to remain consistent.","locale":"en"},"3221":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#theme-and-accent-color","content":"The accent color is used for buttons, selected states, and emphasized information. After choosing a color, check that normal text, selected items, warnings, and links all remain easy to distinguish. If the result is unsuitable, use **Restore defaults** at the bottom of the Appearance page.","locale":"en"},"3222":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#import-images","content":"Click **Add** and select one or more images. You can also drag images from the system file manager into the wallpaper area. The application copies usable images into its own appearance-resources directory.","locale":"en"},"3223":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#check-import-results","content":"Wait for the thumbnails and image dimensions to appear. If some files fail, the page lists their filenames and errors while preserving the other successfully imported images.","locale":"en"},"3224":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#select-wallpaper","content":"Click a thumbnail to select it, then enable **Show background image**. If a resource has been lost, its entry is marked as missing and cannot be used as a valid background.","locale":"en"},"3225":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#choose-fixed-or-random-wallpaper","content":"With **Random wallpaper** off, the selected image is always used. When enabled, the application selects an image at random from the available wallpapers on every startup. The option is unavailable when there are too few resources.","locale":"en"},"3226":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#choose-fixed-or-random-wallpaper","content":"Deleting an individual wallpaper or using **Clear all** removes the application's stored copy, not the original image at the location from which it was imported. Conversely, moving the original usually does not affect a copy that was imported successfully.","locale":"en"},"3227":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"3228":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Recommendation","locale":"en"},"3229":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Interface opacity","locale":"en"},"3230":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Range: 40%–100%; lower values reveal more wallpaper","locale":"en"},"3231":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Glass blur","locale":"en"},"3232":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Range: 0–32; set to 0 to disable blur","locale":"en"},"3233":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Cover","locale":"en"},"3234":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Fills the window and may crop image edges","locale":"en"},"3235":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Contain","locale":"en"},"3236":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Shows the complete image and may leave empty areas when aspect ratios differ","locale":"en"},"3237":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Stretch","locale":"en"},"3238":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Fills the window exactly and may distort the image; **Image position** has no effect","locale":"en"},"3239":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Image position","locale":"en"},"3240":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Determines which area is prioritized when Cover crops or Contain leaves empty space","locale":"en"},"3241":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"Increase interface opacity or blur for high-contrast or visually detailed wallpaper. After\nconfiguring it, check text, errors, and status notices on at least the Home page, settings window,\ninstance management, and dialogs.","locale":"en"},"3242":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-appearance","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-appearance#adjusting-background-effects","content":"If wallpaper fails to display, first confirm that the entry is not marked **Missing**, then try importing it again. Do not directly edit wallpaper files in the application data directory; the resource record may remain after the file becomes unusable.","locale":"en"},"3243":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","type":"page","content":"Diagnostics","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","locale":"en"},"3244":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","content":"Generate, inspect, and export application-level diagnostic bundles.","locale":"en"},"3245":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"Generating application diagnostics","locale":"en"},"3246":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#whether-to-include-all-instances","content":"Whether to include all instances","locale":"en"},"3247":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"What a diagnostic bundle contains","locale":"en"},"3248":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","content":"Application diagnostics are suited to initial-startup, runtime-preparation, cross-instance task, Agent, and platform problems. For an environment or maintenance problem affecting one instance, first generate a smaller bundle from Instance Diagnostics in instance management.","locale":"en"},"3249":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"Reproduce the problem first and record when it happened, the operation, and the related\ninstance.","locale":"en"},"3250":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"Open **Settings → Diagnostics** and decide whether to enable **Include all instances in\napplication diagnostics**.","locale":"en"},"3251":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"Click **Start collection** and watch progress in the lower-right corner of the settings window.\nSwitching sections does not cancel collection.","locale":"en"},"3252":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"After the task finishes, refresh the list and inspect the filename, creation time, size, and\nissue count.","locale":"en"},"3253":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#generating-application-diagnostics","content":"Click **Export** to save a copy to a chosen location, or **Open folder** to view the original\nZIP stored by the application.","locale":"en"},"3254":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#whether-to-include-all-instances","content":"When enabled, the application freezes an instance list at the start of collection and processes each instance in order. Instances created during collection are not appended. If an instance is inaccessible, undergoing maintenance, or has been replaced, the diagnostic manifest records the issue without discarding other content already collected.","locale":"en"},"3255":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#whether-to-include-all-instances","content":"When disabled, the application bundle collects only application-level configuration, logs, status, non-credential Agent data, application tasks, and similar content. It is faster to generate and smaller.","locale":"en"},"3256":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Application diagnostics usually include:","locale":"en"},"3257":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Current global settings and the configuration directory.","locale":"en"},"3258":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"File logs and the in-memory log for the current run.","locale":"en"},"3259":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Application state, task activity, and diagnostics status.","locale":"en"},"3260":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Agent history, memory, and non-sensitive Skill state.","locale":"en"},"3261":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"When instance collection is enabled, instance snapshots, environment reports, tasks, and runtime state.","locale":"en"},"3262":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Provider credential documents and MCP credential documents are excluded in their entirety, but other content is not automatically masked or rewritten. Paths, environment variables, commands, output, tokens, or user data may still appear in other raw sources.","locale":"en"},"3263":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Before sharing, extract the ZIP and inspect `manifest.json`, logs, environment reports, and task\noutput. Remove or mask anything that should not be public, and send the bundle only to a trusted\nrecipient.","locale":"en"},"3264":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-diagnostics#what-a-diagnostic-bundle-contains","content":"Diagnostic ZIP files have no automatic retention period and are not deleted by the log-retention policy. Once they are no longer needed, remove old files from the application diagnostics directory with the system file manager.","locale":"en"},"3265":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","type":"page","content":"Environment Tools","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","locale":"en"},"3266":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","content":"Configure uv, pre-launch environment checks, and CUDA memory optimization.","locale":"en"},"3267":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-uv","content":"Enabling uv","locale":"en"},"3268":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-environment-checks","content":"Enabling environment checks","locale":"en"},"3269":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"Enabling CUDA memory optimization","locale":"en"},"3270":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"Changing and verifying settings","locale":"en"},"3271":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","content":"Environment tools determine how installation flows and WebUI startup use an instance's Python. They do not select the application Python version and do not replace PyTorch, extension, or version operations in instance management.","locale":"en"},"3272":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-uv","content":"When enabled, supported Python package installations use uv instead of pip and are usually faster. If an installation script or non-standard package is incompatible with uv, temporarily disable it and retry the same operation.","locale":"en"},"3273":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-uv","content":"Disabling uv does not uninstall installed packages or automatically restore a previous environment. It only changes the tool used by subsequent installation commands.","locale":"en"},"3274":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-environment-checks","content":"When enabled, the application checks and repairs WebUI dependencies before launch. Keep it enabled after first launch, a Core update, snapshot restoration, or dependency changes.","locale":"en"},"3275":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-environment-checks","content":"An environment check can add startup time. Disable it temporarily only after confirming that the instance environment is complete and when comparing whether the check itself causes startup failure. Enable it again after troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"3276":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"This option requests the CUDA asynchronous memory allocator when launching a WebUI:","locale":"en"},"3277":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"It takes effect only in NVIDIA environments that support the capability.","locale":"en"},"3278":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"AMD, Intel, Apple, and CPU environments ignore it.","locale":"en"},"3279":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"Some older drivers, CUDA versions, or particular WebUI combinations may be incompatible.","locale":"en"},"3280":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#enabling-cuda-memory-optimization","content":"If a CUDA allocator error occurs during startup, disable this option and relaunch the instance for comparison. Do not change PyTorch and several launch arguments at the same time.","locale":"en"},"3281":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"Change only one of uv, environment checks, or CUDA optimization at a time. Switches save\nautomatically.","locale":"en"},"3282":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"Stop and restart the relevant WebUI so the new startup or installation plan reads the setting.","locale":"en"},"3283":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"Check task output for a change in the installation tool, environment check, or CUDA error.","locale":"en"},"3284":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"If there is no improvement, restore the default and continue inspecting instance dependencies or\nthe GPU environment.","locale":"en"},"3285":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-environment-tools#changing-and-verifying-settings","content":"Environment tools are application-level settings. A change can affect every instance that later\nruns a related flow, so do not leave a necessary check disabled indefinitely to solve a problem in\none instance.","locale":"en"},"3286":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","type":"page","content":"Language","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-language","locale":"en"},"3287":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Follow the system language or choose a Chinese or English interface.","locale":"en"},"3288":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-language#switching-languages","content":"Switching languages","locale":"en"},"3289":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"**Settings → Language** controls the language of Hanafubuki's own interface. It does not change the language of the operating system, a WebUI, or a terminal.","locale":"en"},"3290":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Option","locale":"en"},"3291":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Behavior","locale":"en"},"3292":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Auto (follow system)","locale":"en"},"3293":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Choose Chinese or English according to the operating system's current language","locale":"en"},"3294":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Chinese","locale":"en"},"3295":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Always use Chinese, regardless of system-language changes","locale":"en"},"3296":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"English","locale":"en"},"3297":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language","content":"Always use English, regardless of system-language changes","locale":"en"},"3298":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language#switching-languages","content":"Select &#x2A;*Auto (follow system)**, **Chinese**, or **English**. The option saves automatically.","locale":"en"},"3299":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language#switching-languages","content":"Wait for the save status in the lower-right corner to finish, then inspect the left navigation,\nheadings, and button text.","locale":"en"},"3300":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language#switching-languages","content":"After selecting **Auto**, restart Hanafubuki if you later change the system language, ensuring that every window loads with the new system language.","locale":"en"},"3301":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-language-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-language","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-language#switching-languages","content":"The website documentation and application interface are separate content. Changing the application\nlanguage does not automatically switch documentation already open in a browser.","locale":"en"},"3302":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","type":"page","content":"Logs","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-logs","locale":"en"},"3303":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs","content":"Control log levels, file persistence, rotation size, and retention.","locale":"en"},"3304":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"In-memory and file logs","locale":"en"},"3305":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Field reference","locale":"en"},"3306":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Choosing a log level","locale":"en"},"3307":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"Recommended troubleshooting workflow","locale":"en"},"3308":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs","content":"Logs help troubleshoot application, runtime, task, and platform problems. Keep the default **Info** level for everyday use and temporarily increase detail only when you can reproduce a problem reliably.","locale":"en"},"3309":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"The application always retains a capacity-limited log buffer for the current run, which a diagnostic bundle exports as `session.log`. Disabling **Save logs to files** stops only disk persistence; diagnostics for the current run remain available.","locale":"en"},"3310":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"When file persistence is enabled, logs are written to the `logs` folder in the application data directory:","locale":"en"},"3311":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"The current file is `hanafubuki.log`.","locale":"en"},"3312":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"When it reaches the size limit, it is renamed with a UTC timestamp and a new file continues recording.","locale":"en"},"3313":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"Historical `.log` files older than the retention period are removed.","locale":"en"},"3314":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#in-memory-and-file-logs","content":"The active log, directories, and symbolic links are not deleted by the retention policy.","locale":"en"},"3315":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"3316":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Range or behavior","locale":"en"},"3317":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Save logs to files","locale":"en"},"3318":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Controls whether logs are persisted to disk","locale":"en"},"3319":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Maximum log size","locale":"en"},"3320":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"1–512 MB; rotation occurs when the limit is reached","locale":"en"},"3321":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Log retention days","locale":"en"},"3322":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"1–365 days; expired historical logs are removed","locale":"en"},"3323":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Log level","locale":"en"},"3324":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Trace, Debug, Info, Warn, Error, or Off","locale":"en"},"3325":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#field-reference","content":"Numeric fields save when you press `Enter` or leave the input. The size limit cannot be edited while file persistence is disabled; the retention period still applies to historical logs that already exist on disk.","locale":"en"},"3326":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Level","locale":"en"},"3327":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Recommended use","locale":"en"},"3328":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Info","locale":"en"},"3329":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Everyday use; preserves key phases and errors","locale":"en"},"3330":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Debug","locale":"en"},"3331":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Troubleshooting flows and state changes","locale":"en"},"3332":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Trace","locale":"en"},"3333":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Briefly reproducing the hardest problems; contains the most detail","locale":"en"},"3334":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Warn","locale":"en"},"3335":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-32","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Focusing only on anomalies and potential problems","locale":"en"},"3336":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-33","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Error","locale":"en"},"3337":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-34","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Recording failures only","locale":"en"},"3338":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-35","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Off","locale":"en"},"3339":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-36","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"Produces no ordinary logs and is unsuitable for troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"3340":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-37","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#choosing-a-log-level","content":"`trace` may record length-limited Agent requests, reasoning or tool content, as well as path,\nenvironment, and command information. Enable it briefly only when explicitly needed. Restore\n**Info** after reproducing the problem, and inspect logs or diagnostic bundles for sensitive\ncontent before sharing.","locale":"en"},"3341":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-38","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"First reproduce the problem at the default **Info** level and inspect the direct error in the\ntask center.","locale":"en"},"3342":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-39","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"If the information is insufficient, switch to **Debug**. Use **Trace** only if the cause is\nstill unclear.","locale":"en"},"3343":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-40","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"Record the exact reproduction time and steps, then generate a diagnostic bundle immediately\nafter the problem occurs.","locale":"en"},"3344":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-41","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"Restore the original log level to avoid continued growth in disk usage and sensitive-content\nscope.","locale":"en"},"3345":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-logs-42","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-logs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-logs#recommended-troubleshooting-workflow","content":"<Card title=\"Logs, Diagnostics, and Getting Help\" href=\"/docs/troubleshooting-reporting\" description=\"Extract the core error and prepare material maintainers can analyze.\" />","locale":"en"},"3346":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"page","content":"Mirrors","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","locale":"en"},"3347":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","content":"Configure Micromamba, PyPI, GitHub, Hugging Face, and model download sources.","locale":"en"},"3348":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Automatic and manual modes","locale":"en"},"3349":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Recommended configuration order","locale":"en"},"3350":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","content":"Mirrors can improve package and resource download speeds on particular networks, but their contents may be delayed or incomplete. Most users should begin with **Automatically select mirrors** and switch to manual settings only when a fixed source is required or while troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"3351":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"When **Automatically select mirrors** is enabled, the application resolves Micromamba channels for the current network and delegates its automatic policy for supported software sources to the Python installation flow. Manual switches and custom addresses are disabled in this mode, preventing both strategies from applying at once.","locale":"en"},"3352":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"After disabling automatic selection, you can control:","locale":"en"},"3353":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"3354":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Main purpose","locale":"en"},"3355":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Micromamba mirror","locale":"en"},"3356":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Packages and channels for the Conda environment, Git, and other managed tools","locale":"en"},"3357":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"PyPI mirror","locale":"en"},"3358":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Installation of WebUI Python dependencies","locale":"en"},"3359":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"GitHub mirror","locale":"en"},"3360":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Core, extensions, and release resources","locale":"en"},"3361":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Hugging Face mirror","locale":"en"},"3362":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Hugging Face repositories and files","locale":"en"},"3363":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Model download source","locale":"en"},"3364":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"Choose between ModelScope and Hugging Face","locale":"en"},"3365":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#automatic-and-manual-modes","content":"You can enter a custom GitHub or Hugging Face address only after disabling automatic selection and enabling the corresponding manual mirror.","locale":"en"},"3366":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"First verify the connection method under **Network and Proxy** so you do not mistake a proxy\nproblem for a mirror problem.","locale":"en"},"3367":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Keep automatic mirrors enabled and retry the failed task once, recording the destination source\nand error in task output.","locale":"en"},"3368":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If you truly need a fixed source, disable automatic mirrors and change only the setting related\nto the failed resource.","locale":"en"},"3369":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"Run the same task again and check whether the error changes and the actual source is available.","locale":"en"},"3370":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If versions, commits, or checksums disagree, disable the relevant mirror and verify against the\nofficial source.","locale":"en"},"3371":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"The model download source affects only operations using the built-in model downloader. It does not move existing models or change the source from which extensions are downloaded through Git.","locale":"en"},"3372":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"A mirror may omit the latest commit, return a different file, or synchronize late. If an\ninstallation result is abnormal, retry from the official source and review task output. Do not\ndisable verification to accept a mismatched file.","locale":"en"},"3373":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-mirrors#recommended-configuration-order","content":"If every source fails to connect, inspect system time, DNS, proxy, and firewall first. If only one type of resource fails, inspect its corresponding mirror or change the model download source.","locale":"en"},"3374":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"page","content":"Network and Proxy","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network","locale":"en"},"3375":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network","content":"Configure the system proxy, a manual proxy, or a direct connection.","locale":"en"},"3376":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"Choosing a proxy mode","locale":"en"},"3377":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Configuring a manual proxy","locale":"en"},"3378":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network","content":"Proxy settings control how backend downloads, hosted services, and subsequently launched tasks and terminals access the network. They are independent of mirror settings: a proxy determines **how to connect**, while a mirror determines **which source to connect to**.","locale":"en"},"3379":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"The application reads the operating system's current proxy and displays the detected effective\naddress below. If no address is detected, it shows **No system proxy detected** and related\nconnections proceed directly.","locale":"en"},"3380":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"All relevant network operations use the proxy URL you enter. This is useful when the system\nproxy cannot be detected or when only Hanafubuki should use a particular proxy.","locale":"en"},"3381":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#choosing-a-proxy-mode","content":"Ignore both system and manual proxies and connect directly. Use this for a direct network or to\ndetermine whether a failure is caused by an incorrect proxy.","locale":"en"},"3382":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"The manual address must include a protocol, host, and explicit port, for example:","locale":"en"},"3383":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Supported protocols are `http`, `https`, `socks`, `socks4`, `socks4a`, `socks5`, and `socks5h`. An address containing only `127.0.0.1`, no port, or a protocol such as `ftp` is rejected.","locale":"en"},"3384":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Start the proxy application and confirm that it works, noting its listening protocol and port.","locale":"en"},"3385":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Select **Manual** and enter the complete proxy URL. The mode and address are validated together.","locale":"en"},"3386":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"Wait for the save to succeed in the lower-right corner, then run a small update check or\ndownload task.","locale":"en"},"3387":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"If it fails, switch to **Disabled** for a direct-connection comparison before deciding whether\nto inspect the proxy or mirror.","locale":"en"},"3388":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"A proxy snapshot applies to child processes created afterward. An already-running WebUI, task, or ordinary terminal retains the environment from its startup. After changing the proxy, stop and recreate those processes; merely refreshing the page is insufficient.","locale":"en"},"3389":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-network-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-network","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-network#configuring-a-manual-proxy","content":"If the proxy URL contains a username or password, do not copy the complete address into public\nlogs, screenshots, or issue reports. Inspect a diagnostic bundle before sharing it as well.","locale":"en"},"3390":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"page","content":"Paths","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","locale":"en"},"3391":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","content":"Manage the artifact cache, default installation directory, and managed runtime storage.","locale":"en"},"3392":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Cache and default installation directory","locale":"en"},"3393":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Managed runtime storage","locale":"en"},"3394":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#migrating-managed-runtime-storage","content":"Migrating managed runtime storage","locale":"en"},"3395":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#enter-a-new-directory","content":"Enter a new directory","locale":"en"},"3396":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#preview-component-locations","content":"Preview component locations","locale":"en"},"3397":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#schedule-migration","content":"Schedule migration","locale":"en"},"3398":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#exit-normally-and-restart","content":"Exit normally and restart","locale":"en"},"3399":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result","locale":"en"},"3400":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths","content":"The Paths page contains two kinds of locations: ordinary downloads and instance defaults, and runtime storage maintained by the application itself. They serve different purposes, and changing one does not automatically migrate another.","locale":"en"},"3401":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-10","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Setting","locale":"en"},"3402":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-11","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Effect","locale":"en"},"3403":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-12","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Artifact cache directory","locale":"en"},"3404":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-13","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Location where future installation and download tasks save and reuse downloaded artifacts","locale":"en"},"3405":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-14","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Default WebUI installation directory","locale":"en"},"3406":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-15","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Root directory prefilled when creating a new instance; does not move or rewrite existing instances","locale":"en"},"3407":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-16","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"These two fields must be saved manually. The backend validates and prepares the directories during save, so do not press `Enter` before you have finished entering a path.","locale":"en"},"3408":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-17","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Enter a path or use the directory picker. Check that you did not select a system directory or\nanother instance's component directory.","locale":"en"},"3409":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-18","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Create an instance or rerun a download task and confirm that the page uses the new default\nlocation.","locale":"en"},"3410":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-19","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#cache-and-default-installation-directory","content":"Changing the artifact cache does not move the old cache or delete its original directory. After confirming that new tasks work, use the system file manager to assess whether the old cache can be removed.","locale":"en"},"3411":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-20","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Managed runtime storage is maintained by Hanafubuki itself and contains:","locale":"en"},"3412":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-21","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The application's Standalone Python.","locale":"en"},"3413":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-22","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The Micromamba executable.","locale":"en"},"3414":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-23","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"The Conda root directory and package cache.","locale":"en"},"3415":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-24","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"Verified Launcher Python code.","locale":"en"},"3416":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#managed-runtime-storage","content":"It does not contain WebUI instances, models, the ordinary artifact cache, or diagnostic bundles. To change only where new instances are located, edit **Default WebUI installation directory** instead of migrating the managed runtime.","locale":"en"},"3417":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#enter-a-new-directory","content":"The final destination must be a new directory that does not yet exist. It cannot overlap application data, an existing instance, or a component path, and its path cannot traverse a symbolic link. After using Browse to select a parent directory, you can append a new child-directory name in the input.","locale":"en"},"3418":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#preview-component-locations","content":"Click **Migrate** and inspect the Python, Micromamba, Conda, and Launcher Code destinations in the confirmation dialog. This creates only a plan and does not copy files yet.","locale":"en"},"3419":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#schedule-migration","content":"Click **Migrate on next restart**. The page records the pending destination. If you have not exited the application, you can use **Cancel** to withdraw this scheduled plan.","locale":"en"},"3420":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#exit-normally-and-restart","content":"Finish running instances, terminals, and maintenance tasks first, then exit the application normally. On restart, the startup page completes migration before loading other features.","locale":"en"},"3421":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"After the application opens, return to **Paths** and **Runtime**. Confirm the current runtime root and the states of Python, Micromamba, and Git.","locale":"en"},"3422":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-31","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"Migration does not merge runtime content into an existing directory. During migration, do not move\nthe source directory, create the destination in advance, or start a second Hanafubuki process.","locale":"en"},"3423":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-paths-32","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-paths","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-paths#verify-the-result","content":"If migration fails, the application continues using the original location if it remains valid and displays a recovery record. Resolve disk-space, permission, or destination-conflict problems, click **Retry**, then exit and start normally. Do not directly delete the source directory or staged destination content.","locale":"en"},"3424":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"page","content":"Runtime","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","locale":"en"},"3425":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","content":"Inspect and configure the application's Python, Micromamba, and Git.","locale":"en"},"3426":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Reading the status panels","locale":"en"},"3427":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-application-python","content":"Choosing application Python","locale":"en"},"3428":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"Choosing a Git source","locale":"en"},"3429":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Troubleshooting failures","locale":"en"},"3430":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","content":"The Runtime page displays the Python, Micromamba, and Git that Hanafubuki itself depends on. These are application-level runtimes and are independent of each WebUI instance's own Python and Core.","locale":"en"},"3431":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Each panel shows the current status, preparation step, errors, and detected information:","locale":"en"},"3432":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-7","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Panel","locale":"en"},"3433":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-8","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Important information","locale":"en"},"3434":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-9","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#reading-the-status-panels","content":"Appli