git-source","content":"Skip system Git and always use the application-managed Git","locale":"en"},"3450":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-25","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#choosing-a-git-source","content":"The Git source also takes effect on the next application startup. Keep the default when the system already has a usable Git installation. Choose Micromamba when you need a fixed, isolated Git environment.","locale":"en"},"3451":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-26","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Python download or verification failure: inspect the network, proxy, mirrors, disk space, and managed-runtime directory permissions.","locale":"en"},"3452":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-27","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Micromamba failure: confirm that a second application process is not using the runtime and that the destination disk is writable.","locale":"en"},"3453":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-28","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Git waiting for Micromamba: let Micromamba finish preparing first; this is not an independent Git hang.","locale":"en"},"3454":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-29","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Status subscription unavailable: use Retry on the panel; if it still fails, generate an application diagnostic bundle.","locale":"en"},"3455":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime-30","page_id":"/en/docs/settings-runtime","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings-runtime#troubleshooting-failures","content":"Do not overwrite managed Python, Micromamba, Conda, or Launcher Code from outside the application.\nHanafubuki prepares these components according to its own versions and verification rules, and may\nidentify manual changes as corruption during the next check.","locale":"en"},"3456":{"id":"/en/docs/settings","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"page","content":"Settings","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","Settings"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings","locale":"en"},"3457":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-0","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings","content":"Understand how settings are saved and configure Hanafubuki by section.","locale":"en"},"3458":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-1","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"How settings are saved","locale":"en"},"3459":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-2","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/settings#finding-settings-by-section","content":"Finding settings by section","locale":"en"},"3460":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-3","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings","content":"The settings window manages options that apply across the application. The sections on the left correspond one-to-one with this documentation directory. Change an instance's own paths, launch arguments, and maintenance options in instance management instead.","locale":"en"},"3461":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-4","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Different field types use different save behavior:","locale":"en"},"3462":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-5","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Field type","locale":"en"},"3463":{"id":"/en/docs/settings-6","page_id":"/en/docs/settings","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/settings#how-settings-are-saved","content":"Save behavior","locale":"en"},"3464":{"id":"/en/doc