","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#preserve-the-complete-error","content":"Preserve the complete error","locale":"en"},"3792":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-5","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#determine-where-the-error-belongs","content":"Determine where the error belongs","locale":"en"},"3793":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-6","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#collect-diagnostics-if-it-remains-unresolved","content":"Collect diagnostics if it remains unresolved","locale":"en"},"3794":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-7","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Where did the error occur?","locale":"en"},"3795":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-8","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#how-to-tell-whether-webui-has-started","content":"How to tell whether WebUI has started","locale":"en"},"3796":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-9","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#read-the-error-before-choosing-an-action","content":"Read the error before choosing an action","locale":"en"},"3797":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-10","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#when-to-stop-trying-more-changes","content":"When to stop trying more changes","locale":"en"},"3798":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-11","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#quick-links","content":"Quick links","locale":"en"},"3799":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-12","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"The most important first step in troubleshooting is to determine whether the failure occurred in Hanafubuki, the installation environment, instance startup, or inside a running WebUI. Each layer uses different logs, retry procedures, and support channels.","locale":"en"},"3800":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-13","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","content":"Cancellation, stopping, and cleanup all require the backend to confirm a terminal state. Retrying\nwhile an old task is still running or awaiting cleanup can continue to occupy the instance, port,\nor files, and may let new logs obscure the true first error.","locale":"en"},"3801":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-14","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#stop-repeating-the-operation","content":"Do not continue starting, installing, or deleting. Record the current page, instance name, time, and operation you just performed.","locale":"en"},"3802":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-15","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#find-the-first-failed-task","content":"First expand the bottom-right status item on the current page, then open Task Center in the title bar. Select the earliest related failure instead of looking only at subsequent cascading failures.","locale":"en"},"3803":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-16","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#preserve-the-complete-error","content":"Copy the task output or terminal log. Preserve the surrounding context, the final Python traceback block, and the command exit status instead of capturing only a one-line error heading.","locale":"en"},"3804":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-17","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#determine-where-the-error-belongs","content":"Use the &#x2A;*Where did the error occur?** table below to open the relevant topic. Change one relevant setting at a time, then repeat the same operation to verify it.","locale":"en"},"3805":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-18","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#collect-diagnostics-if-it-remains-unresolved","content":"After reproducing the issue, generate an instance or application diagnostic bundle. Extract, inspect, and redact it before sharing, and include the reproduction steps, versions, and complete logs.","locale":"en"},"3806":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-19","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Symptom","locale":"en"},"3807":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-20","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Usual layer","locale":"en"},"3808":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-21","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Next step","locale":"en"},"3809":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-22","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Hanafubuki will not open normally, or application Python, Micromamba, or Git is not ready","locale":"en"},"3810":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-23","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Application runtime","locale":"en"},"3811":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-24","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"Application and Runtime Environment","locale":"en"},"3812":{"id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting-25","page_id":"/en/docs/troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/troubleshooting#where-did-the-error-occur","content":"