ting-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#before-importing","content":"If you have only WebUI Core and no suitable Python, do not force an import. Use Scan the\nSystem. A recognized Core becomes an instance awaiting installation, and\nHanafubuki then prepares managed Python for it.","locale":"en"},"3890":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#select-the-import-source","content":"On Home, select **Add instance**, then switch the source at the top to **Import existing instance**.","locale":"en"},"3891":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#select-the-correct-webui-type","content":"Select the type used by the existing project. This determines launch arguments and management features; Hanafubuki does not convert one WebUI into another.","locale":"en"},"3892":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#set-the-name-and-root-directory","content":"You may leave the instance name blank to generate one automatically. **Existing instance root** must be an existing directory.","locale":"en"},"3893":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#confirm-the-python-directory","content":"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/python`. If Python is elsewhere, select its actual root. The application checks that it is usable before saving the record.","locale":"en"},"3894":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#confirm-the-core-directory","content":"For a standard layout, leave it blank to use `<root>/core`. If the existing root is itself WebUI Core, explicitly select the root as the Core directory.","locale":"en"},"3895":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#import-and-verify","content":"Select **Import instance**. After success, the instance workspace opens and begins preparing management services and starting WebUI. You can then verify all three directories under **Instance Management → Component Paths**.","locale":"en"},"3896":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Creates a Hanafubuki instance record and default launch arguments.","locale":"en"},"3897":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Leaves the existing root, Python, and Core in their original locations without copying or moving them.","locale":"en"},"3898":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Does not install or update Python packages, Core, extensions, or models as part of the import itself.","locale":"en"},"3899":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"Allows later version switching, extension management, terminal commands, and reinstallation to modify the original files.","locale":"en"},"3900":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing-37","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-import-existing#what-importing-changes","content":"**Delete instance** deletes the ver