ce-families","content":"**Automatic** leaves the build unpinned so that the current installer can choose for the environment.","locale":"en"},"3983":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-70","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"Pin an option manually only when you know the GPU driver, CUDA, ROCm, or CPU requirements.","locale":"en"},"3984":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-71","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#pytorch-builds-and-device-families","content":"Selecting an incompatible build manually may let installation succeed while leaving the GPU unavailable at startup.","locale":"en"},"3985":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-72","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#branches","content":"Stable Diffusion WebUI, Fooocus, and SD Trainer can select a branch preset returned by the installation catalog. Stable Diffusion WebUI resolves **Default branch** to `sd_webui_forge_neo`; the Fooocus and SD Trainer defaults add no override. A selected branch becomes the baseline for later instance reinstallation and version management.","locale":"en"},"3986":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-73","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Each predownload option has three states:","locale":"en"},"3987":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-74","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Selection","locale":"en"},"3988":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-75","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"3989":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-76","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Use installer default","locale":"en"},"3990":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-77","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Do not force enablement or disablement; let the current WebUI installer decide","locale":"en"},"3991":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-78","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Enabled","locale":"en"},"3992":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-79","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Explicitly require the installer to perform the predownload","locale":"en"},"3993":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-80","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Disabled","locale":"en"},"3994":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-81","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Explicitly require the installer to skip the predownload","locale":"en"},"3995":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-82","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"Predownloading can reduce the wait after first startup, but it increases installation time, network traffic, and disk usage. It does not make the installation offline: source code, Python packages, and other dependencies may still require downloads.","locale":"en"},"3996":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options-83","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-options","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-options#predownload-models-and-extensions","content":"New users should retain the type-default Python, automatic device, default branch, and\ninstaller-default predownloads. Change one option at a time only when a specific compatibility\nrequirement arises, then verify again.","locale":"en"},"3997":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","type":"page","content":"Installation Progress and Troubleshooting","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","WebUI Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","locale":"en"},"3998":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","content":"Inspect installation stages, logs, and cancellation state, then perform cleanup and retries correctly.","locale":"en"},"3999":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting#understand-installation-stages","content":"Understand installation stages","locale":"en"},"4000":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting#inspect-and-preserve-output","content":"Inspect and preserve output","locale":"en"},"4001":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting#cancel-clean-up-and-retry","content":"Cancel, clean up, and retry","locale":"en"},"4002":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-install-troubleshooting","type":"heading","tags"