w-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#select-a-webui-type","content":"Select Stable Diffusion WebUI, ComfyUI, InvokeAI, Fooocus, SD Trainer, or Qwen TTS WebUI on the left. The preview on the right only helps identify the product; the selected type determines the actual installation and management rules.","locale":"en"},"4124":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#continue-to-configuration","content":"Select **Next**. The application loads the currently available branch and PyTorch options together. If loading fails, use **Reload options** without selecting the WebUI again.","locale":"en"},"4125":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#set-the-instance-name","content":"**Instance name** is shown on Home and in Instance Management. You may leave it blank, in which case the application generates a name from the WebUI product name with a random suffix.","locale":"en"},"4126":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#confirm-the-installation-root","content":"Leaving **Installation root** blank is recommended. The application uses the global default directory shown in Settings and creates a dedicated directory named with the instance ID beneath it.","locale":"en"},"4127":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#confirm-the-installation-root","content":"If you select a directory manually, that directory itself becomes the final instance root; another nested directory is not created automatically. Use a new, dedicated directory. Do not select a drive root, your home directory, or an existing directory containing important files.","locale":"en"},"4128":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#select-a-branch","content":"**Branch** appears only for WebUIs that support branch presets. Most users should select **Default branch**. Switch only when you specifically need a prerelease or variant.","locale":"en"},"4129":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#review-advanced-options","content":"Expand **Advanced options** to change the Python/Core subdirectories, Python version, PyTorch build, and predownload settings. The defaults already form a working installation plan; do not change an option you do not understand.","locale":"en"},"4130":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#review-advanced-options","content":"Python must reside inside the instance root, and a newly created Core directory should also stay inside it. If you explicitly select a verified existing external Core, the installer may reuse and update it, but cannot force-rebuild that external directory. Use Scan the System when you are unsure where an existing Core is located.","locale":"en"},"4131":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#create-and-install","content":"Select **Create and install**. The application first saves the instance record, then opens that instance's installation workspace and prepares Python and WebUI Core in sequence. Do not manually move or delete directories during installation.","locale":"en"},"4132":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#wait-for-automatic-startup","content":"After installation, the workspace continues preparing management services and starts WebUI automatically. You can use it once a startup address is captured. If startup requires a PyTorch decision or dependency-conflict resolution, the workspace displays the corresponding decision.","locale":"en"},"4133":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"Each WebUI determines its own model, extension, and output directories, so they do not necessarily share one location. Before changing advanced settings, read Installation Options in Detail.","locale":"en"},"4134":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"In rare cases, the instance record is created but the installation task cannot start. The instance\nis not lost: reopen it and select **Start installation** in the workspace to continue.","locale":"en"},"4135":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-new-installation#default-directory-layout","content":"If installation fails or progress does not change for a long time, see Installation Progress and Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"4136":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"page","content":"Scan for Existing WebUIs","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","WebUI Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","locale":"en"},"4137":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","content":"Scan the computer or a selected folder to discover and attach existing WebUIs automatically.","locale":"en"},"4138":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Two scan scopes","locale":"en"},"4139":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#scan-steps","content":"Scan steps","locale":"en"},"4140":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#select-scan-system","content":"Select Scan system","locale":"en"},"4141":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-and-confirm-the-scan-scope","content":"Review and confirm the scan scope","locale":"en"},"4142":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-5","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#return-to-home-and-wait","content":"Return to Home and wait","locale":"en"},"4143":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-6","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-the-completion-summary","content":"Review the completion summary","locale":"en"},"4144":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-7","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"Handle instances awaiting installation","locale":"en"},"4145":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-8","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"What the summary results mean","locale":"en"},"4146":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-9","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Why an instance was not found","locale":"en"},"4147":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-10","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","content":"Scanning is appropriate when you do not know an instance's path, or when only WebUI Core exists without a usable standalone Python. Scanning identifies the WebUI type from marker files in its directory, so you do not need to select a type first.","locale":"en"},"4148":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-11","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Select **Scan system** on the **Add instance** page. Windows scans fixed disks on the computer;\nLinux and macOS scan the current filesystem beginning at the system root. A full scan may read\nmany directories and take several minutes.","locale":"en"},"4149":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-12","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#two-scan-scopes","content":"Drag a folder from the file manager onto Hanafubuki Home to scan only that directory. This is\nfaster when WebUI resides on an external disk, in a mounted directory, or near a known location,\nand it more easily avoids full-system scan-scope limitations.","locale":"en"},"4150":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-13","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#select-scan-system","content":"Select **Add instance** on Home, then switch to **Scan system**. This mode has no WebUI type list or second-step configuration form.","locale":"en"},"4151":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-and-confirm-the-scan-scope","content":"Selecting **Scan this computer** opens a confirmation window describing the estimated duration, automatic-add behavior, and background execution. A full-system scan starts only after confirmation.","locale":"en"},"4152":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#return-to-home-and-wait","content":"The page returns to Home while scanning continues in the background. The bottom status report first shows directories read and candidates found, then shows the number processed during the attachment stage.","locale":"en"},"4153":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#review-the-completion-summary","content":"The completion report lists counts for added, awaiting installation, already existing, and skipped items. Scanning does not ask for confirmation on each candidate; qualifying projects appear on Home automatically.","locale":"en"},"4154":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"If only Core is found without usable Python, the instance displays **Not installed**. Open it and select **Start installation**. The application prepares Python in a new managed instance root while continuing to use the discovered external Core.","locale":"en"},"4155":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#handle-instances-awaiting-installation","content":"Scanning and attachment only read existing files and write instance records. Installing an\ninstance that is **Awaiting installation** runs the complete installer against the discovered Core\nand may download, update, or adjust its files. Back up custom code first.","locale":"en"},"4156":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Result","locale":"en"},"4157":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Meaning","locale":"en"},"4158":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Next step","locale":"en"},"4159":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Added","locale":"en"},"4160":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Both Core and standalone Python are usable; the instance is ready","locale":"en"},"4161":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open the instance and verify startup","locale":"en"},"4162":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Awaiting installation","locale":"en"},"4163":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Core was recognized, but no unique, usable standalone Python was found","locale":"en"},"4164":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open the instance and start installation","locale":"en"},"4165":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Already exists","locale":"en"},"4166":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"The same Core is already managed by an instance","locale":"en"},"4167":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Use the existing instance; do not add it again","locale":"en"},"4168":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Skipped","locale":"en"},"4169":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"The candidate did not meet a condition during attachment or validation","locale":"en"},"4170":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Open Task Center for the exact reason","locale":"en"},"4171":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-34","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"Detailed Task Center results may also include:","locale":"en"},"4172":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-35","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Path conflict**: The candidate root, Python, or Core overlaps an existing instance.","locale":"en"},"4173":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-36","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Invalid Python**: A possible Python was found, but it could not execute or its version could not be parsed.","locale":"en"},"4174":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-37","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Access warning**: A subdirectory could not be read; scanning continues with other directories.","locale":"en"},"4175":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-38","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Root failure**: The selected scan root itself could not be read. The entire scan fails if every root fails.","locale":"en"},"4176":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-39","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#what-the-summary-results-mean","content":"**Processing failure**: Path safety, instance-record, or lifecycle-commit steps did not complete.","locale":"en"},"4177":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-40","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Scanning recognizes only currently supported directory markers and deliberately skips symbolic links and Windows reparse points. On Unix systems, a full-system scan does not cross into another filesystem, so scan an external disk or certain mount directories by dragging in the folder. Highly customized layouts may also prevent Python from being associated automatically; in that case, import the instance manually.","locale":"en"},"4178":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system-41","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-scan-system#why-an-instance-was-not-found","content":"Open Task Center to inspect scan paths, warnings, and exact results. If the cause remains unclear, see Installation Troubleshooting.","locale":"en"},"4179":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"page","content":"Restore from a Snapshot","breadcrumbs":["Hanafubuki Documentation","WebUI Installation"],"tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","locale":"en"},"4180":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-0","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","content":"Create and rebuild a new WebUI instance from an environment snapshot JSON file.","locale":"en"},"4181":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-1","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"Obtain the snapshot file","locale":"en"},"4182":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-2","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Compatibility checks before restoration","locale":"en"},"4183":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-3","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#create-the-restored-instance","content":"Create the restored instance","locale":"en"},"4184":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-4","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-snapshot-restoration","content":"Select snapshot restoration","locale":"en"},"4185":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-5","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-webui-type","content":"Select the WebUI type","locale":"en"},"4186":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-6","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#set-the-name-and-root","content":"Set the name and root","locale":"en"},"4187":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-7","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#confirm-python-and-core","content":"Confirm Python and Core","locale":"en"},"4188":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-8","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-snapshot-json","content":"Select the snapshot JSON","locale":"en"},"4189":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-9","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#restore-and-install","content":"Restore and install","locale":"en"},"4190":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-10","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#verify-and-restore-user-data","content":"Verify and restore user data","locale":"en"},"4191":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-11","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#what-a-snapshot-does-and-does-not-include","content":"What a snapshot does and does not include","locale":"en"},"4192":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-12","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","content":"An environment snapshot records recoverable information such as the WebUI type, Python, packages, Core commit, and extensions. It is suitable for recreating an environment or migrating its configuration, but it is not a complete backup of models, outputs, and all user files.","locale":"en"},"4193":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-13","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"In the original instance, open **Instance Management → Snapshots** and select **Create snapshot**. The resulting JSON is located at:","locale":"en"},"4194":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-14","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#obtain-the-snapshot-file","content":"After creation, expand the details to confirm the WebUI type, Python version, packages, extensions, and Core commit. To migrate to another device, copy this JSON yourself along with models, outputs, configuration, and custom files.","locale":"en"},"4195":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-15","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Restoring a new instance validates the snapshot before creating its record:","locale":"en"},"4196":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-16","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Check","locale":"en"},"4197":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-17","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Requirement","locale":"en"},"4198":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-18","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"File","locale":"en"},"4199":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-19","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A valid JSON file no larger than 64 MiB","locale":"en"},"4200":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-20","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Snapshot format","locale":"en"},"4201":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-21","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A currently supported environment snapshot format version","locale":"en"},"4202":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-22","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"WebUI type","locale":"en"},"4203":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-23","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Must match the type selected on the creation page","locale":"en"},"4204":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-24","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Python","locale":"en"},"4205":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-25","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"CPython with a major and minor version supported by the application","locale":"en"},"4206":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-26","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"Platform","locale":"en"},"4207":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-27","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"The Windows, macOS, or Linux platform must be compatible with the current system","locale":"en"},"4208":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-28","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#compatibility-checks-before-restoration","content":"A snapshot does not automatically convert a Python environment across platforms or turn it into another WebUI type.","locale":"en"},"4209":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-29","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-snapshot-restoration","content":"Select **Add instance** on Home, then switch the source to **Restore from snapshot**.","locale":"en"},"4210":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-30","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-webui-type","content":"Select the WebUI to which the snapshot originally belonged. A mismatch is rejected after submission, and no instance with the wrong type is created.","locale":"en"},"4211":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-31","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#set-the-name-and-root","content":"You may leave the name blank. Leave the installation root blank or select a new, dedicated directory. A manually selected directory is the final instance root.","locale":"en"},"4212":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-32","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#confirm-python-and-core","content":"A standard restoration retains the default `<instance root>/python` and `<instance root>/core`. Do not target an existing Core that contains important, unbacked-up changes.","locale":"en"},"4213":{"id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery-33","page_id":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/en/docs/webui-snapshot-recovery#select-the-snapshot-json","content":"Under **Snapshot JSON file**, select the file from the original instance's `snapshots` directory. During instance creation, the original file is read and stored as managed recovery data for the current instance."