mediately rebuild the entire Core."],[2711,"If an extension download fails, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors. To roll back the environment as a whole, use Snapshot Management."],[2640,"If application files are missing or damaged, it downloads them again and repairs them according to the manifest."],[3176,"If automatic installation fails, the application attempts to provide a manual installer. Exit the application completely before installing it normally for the current platform; do not run the old application and installer at the same time."],[2375,"If automatic review fails, times out, or returns a denial, the operation is not executed. Read the reason in the tool card instead of repeatedly submitting the same call."],[3030,"If automatic selection fails, check the graphics driver, operating-system support, and detected device reported by the page. Do not try several CUDA/ROCm builds at random."],[2513,"If cleanup fails, run `/stop` again as directed by the card; do not merely delete the session."],[3373,"If every source fails to connect, inspect system time, DNS, proxy, and firewall first. If only one type of resource fails, inspect its corresponding mirror or change the model download source."],[2641,"If every update source is unavailable, it skips the remote check and launches the version already downloaded."],[2298,"If image reading, decoding, or request admission fails, the text and attachment draft remain available so you can fix the problem and send again."],[4135,"If installation fails or progress does not change for a long time, see Installation Progress and Troubleshooting."],[3387,"If it fails, switch to **Disabled** for a direct-connection comparison before deciding whether\nto inspect the proxy or mirror."],[3613,"If it still fails, collect an instance diagnostic bundle and retain the failed startup activity."],[2709,"If launch fails, disable the most recently changed extension first, then inspect its task output\nand compatibility notes."],[3580,"If manual intervention is truly necessary, use the instance terminal and create a snapshot first."],[3509,"If Micromamba is not ready, resolve that first. Git waiting for Micromamba does not mean Git\nitself is damaged."],[3423,"If migration fails, the application continues using the original location if it remains valid and displays a recovery record. Resolve disk-space, permission, or destination-conflict problems, click **Retry**, then exit and start normally. Do not directly delete the source directory or staged destination content."],[3716,"If migration, reinstallation, or deletion was interrupted, return to **Maintenance** and continue the same recovery operation."],[2275,"If no model is currently selected, click the model button or run `/model` first."],[2734,"If online application is unavailable, stop and relaunch the WebUI, then inspect hotpatch runtime\nstatus under “Instance Information.”"],[4154,"If only Core is found without usable Python, the instance displays **Not installed**. Open it and select **Start installation**. The application prepares Python in a new managed instance root while continuing to use the discovered external Core."],[3505,"If only one instance reports `ModuleNotFoundError`, CUDA, or extension errors when it starts, investigate the instance environment rather than application Python."],[3031,"If package downloads or resolution fail, check Network & Proxy and Mirrors."],[2645,"If preparation fails, go to “Settings → Runtime Environment” to retry or change download sources. You can also read Runtime Environment Troubleshooting."],[2137,"If process cleanup or session relationships still have unmet requirements, the backend rejects the deletion and preserves the data. Resolve the cleanup obligation in the message and retry. Do not interpret a failed deletion as meaning that records were partially removed."],[3578,"If PyTorch installation fails, restore **Automatic** or the type's default option and verify the GPU driver."],[3497,"If recovery still fails"],[3770,"If SD Note does not cover the issue, search official repository issues using the exception type, final-line description, WebUI name, and extension name. Prefer guidance from Core or extension authors, and check which versions and operating systems a solution applies to."],[3522,"If the application is still operable, first record which page has the problem and restart normally. If the issue occurs only in the embedded WebUI, try opening the captured address in an external browser from **Instance information**. This distinguishes a WebUI page issue from an application-window rendering issue."],[2428,"If the configured context window is too high, the server may reject a request first. If it is too low, compaction begins earlier. Compaction changes only the context sent to the model on the next turn; it does not delete messages or tool records saved in the interface."],[2343,"If the current response, compaction, or blocking decision has not finished, resolve that state before switching."],[2518,"If the final response claims completion while a tool is still running or awaiting cleanup, trust the backend state."],[3342,"If the information is insufficient, switch to **Debug**. Use **Trace** only if the cause is\nstill unclear."],[3582,"If the instance record was saved but the task did not start, reopen that instance and select **Start installation**. You do not need to delete the record or recreate an instance with the same name."],[3139,"If the list is empty or fails to refresh, check the network, PyPI mirror, and instance management API."],[3614,"If the log clearly points to an extension, disable, update, or roll back that extension first. If Core and the extension interface are incompatible, check both versions together. Do not uninstall every Python package first; doing so destroys the environment needed for further diagnosis."],[2109,"If the model explicitly reports insufficient context before producing any output, the application may compact and retry. Once output has been produced, it does not automatically replay the entire turn, avoiding duplicate tool calls or external actions."],[3623,"If the old task belongs to Hanafubuki, finish stopping and cleaning up that task before restarting; do not kill the process directly and immediately restart it."],[3633,"If the page opens but generation, model, or node operations fail, startup succeeded. Continue with Upstream WebUI issues."],[2989,"If the page reports that the instance configuration has changed, select “Reload,” choose the directories again, and resubmit. Do not use a stale page to overwrite configuration just saved by another management operation."],[3571,"If the path does not exist, overlaps a dangerous location, passes through a symbolic link, or contains conflicting files, choose a new directory as instructed by the interface."],[3389,"If the proxy URL contains a username or password, do not copy the complete address into public\nlogs, screenshots, or issue reports. Inspect a diagnostic bundle before sharing it as well."],[3134,"If the repository contains uncommitted changes, the interface asks for confirmation. Continuing does not guarantee that those changes will be preserved. Cancel and back them up first if loss or conflicts would be unacceptable."],[3032,"If the result remains incompatible after installation, open the latest task output and record the selected build, exit code, and environment-check result."],[2763,"If the structured catalog cannot be loaded, the page falls back to the raw editor. You can keep and save arguments in that mode, but automatic validation is more limited. Check the management API and Core environment, then use “Retry Discovery.”"],[3835,"If the WebUI address is reachable but a feature inside the page fails, investigate WebUI, extensions, and models before reinstalling Hanafubuki's application runtime."],[2960,"If the WebUI is running but has no address, inspect the launch output for the listening address, port co